  "legacyDialogue": [
    {
      "speaker": "Captain Dain",
      "portrait": "warden",
      "text": "I came without my patrol. The truce holds while I watch from the treeline."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "Bring me to the central grove. I need three quiet nights with the roots; if I must leave, the memory slips away."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "Then we stand around you. The overseer would not send soldiers to silence an empty story."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "The roots have spoken. The Rootbinder killed the woodcutters and raised their bodies to serve the overseer."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Captain Dain",
      "portrait": "warden",
      "text": "I saw his seal on the dead. We fought you on a lie. The villages must hear what happened, even if it costs me my command."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "I will bring their memory and this living branch. Let the households hear the dead and judge the living."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Tamsin",
      "portrait": "adept",
      "text": "I will watch from the treeline. Dain is gone, but the families still deserve to know who killed their woodcutters."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "Then we stand around you. Let the roots answer where swords could not."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Tamsin",
      "portrait": "adept",
      "text": "I saw his seal on the dead. I will take you to the village meeting. Dain’s death cannot excuse what his employer has done."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "The owls found a forgotten patrol cache. Better six coins for a living grove than for another axe."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "The grove needs one night to recover. We hold it until dawn."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Lark",
      "portrait": "thorncaller",
      "text": "The overseer has sent patrols along both roads. One on the third turn, another on the fifth. The wooden forts are theirs only while they stand in them."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Captain Dain",
      "portrait": "warden",
      "text": "I saw the thing under the stones. It wore a dead man’s face and my lord’s seal."
    },
    {
      "speaker": "Alder",
      "portrait": "wildkeeper",
      "text": "Then take our witness to your people. A forest and a village can share a road."
    }
  ]
